---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';

export const prerender = true;
---

<PageLayout
  title="Disclosure"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} makes money — affiliate links, advertising and sponsored content.`}
  lede="How this site makes money, stated plainly."
  updated="October 13, 2026"
>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} is free to read. It is paid for by advertising and affiliate commissions. Here is
    exactly how that works, in line with the US Federal Trade Commission's endorsement guidelines
    and the UK CAP Code.
  </p>

  <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
  <p>
    Some product links may be affiliate links. If you buy through one, Small Cozy Home may receive
    a commission from the retailer at no extra cost to you. Pages with affiliate links should
    identify them near the relevant recommendation.
  </p>
  <p>
    Small Cozy Home participates in the Amazon Services LLC Associates Program. The retailer
    determines its current commission terms. Recommendations and prices should be checked on the
    retailer site before purchase.
  </p>
  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    Google AdSense is enabled only when the site is configured for advertising and consent
    management. If enabled, Google selects the individual ads; their appearance is not an
    endorsement. See our <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a> for information about
    advertising technologies and consent.
  </p>
  <h2>Sponsored content and gifted items</h2>
  <p>
    If a page includes paid or gifted products, the relationship should be identified on that page.
    Contact us if you see a relationship that appears to be missing.
  </p>

  <h2>Photography</h2>
  <p>
    Article images include illustrative stock photography from third-party image services, including
    Unsplash and Pexels. Individual photographer and source links appear with some images. Images
    should not be read as documentation of a project tested or photographed by Small Cozy Home.
    Product images may be owned by the relevant retailer.
  </p>
  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    If anything here is unclear, or you think we have got a disclosure wrong, tell us at
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. We would rather fix it.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
